  "_comment": "liteLLMProviderName matches the `litellm_provider` FIELD in LiteLLM's model_prices_and_context_window.json — never a key prefix. null means LiteLLM catalogues no models for this provider.",
  "_comment_deepseek_endpoint": "DeepSeek's documented base URL is the bare host; `/v1` exists only for OpenAI-SDK compatibility and denotes no version. Both resolve (verified: /models and /v1/models each 401 rather than 404), so the bare form is kept — it is what the endpoint preset has always used, and the two must agree for adoption to fire.",
  "_comment_variants": "A built-in's endpoint is FIXED (only the API key is user-editable), so every endpoint a user might need is its own preset — regional and variant endpoints included. Each entry's endpoint must match its ProviderAPIType.endpointPresets entry byte-for-byte, because seedBuiltInProviders() adopts a user's custom provider into a built-in slot only on an exact (apiType, endpoint) match. BuiltInProviderEndpointPresetParityTests enforces the 1:1 correspondence. Variants share the parent's liteLLMProviderName because they serve the same catalogue.",
